  - key: note.ftuenote1.page0.1
    value: "Once more: to pick up or \ninspect an item, press    .\n\nJust don't
      click everything in sight -\ndon't turn it into a monkey test\n\nBetter approach
      the desk"
  - key: note.ftuenote10.page0.1
    value: "Not every door is open\nNot every one has a key\nUse everything you find\nDon't
      give up!\n\nGo through all the rooms... \nLearn the story...\nFind the way
      out!"
  - key: note.ftuenote3.page0.1
    value: "It is dark here. \nIt will only get darker\n\nFind the flashlight: \nsearch
      the desk drawers\n\nHold        and pull toward you, \ndon't let go!"
  - key: note.ftuenote4.page0.1
    value: "Without batteries it is useless\n\nCheck the shelves\n\nJump! \t\nJump!\n\nYou
      won't want to wander \naround here in the dark"
  - key: note.ftuenote5.page0.1
    value: "         will open the inventory\n\nDrag one item onto another and get
      an item \nwith new properties\n\nDone?\nPress        to turn on the light"
  - key: note.ftuenote6.page0.1
    value: "If something stands in your way -\npush it aside\nDon't let it knock
      you down or stop you\n\nIf something stands in your way -\npush it aside\n\nHold      
      and pull, \ndon't let go!"
  - key: note.ftuenote7.page0.1
    value: 'Don''t forget to look at your feet

      You can even crouch

      Or
      crawl under...'
  - key: note.ftuenote8.page0.1
    value: 'Not everything will lie in plain sight


      Some things are hidden


      Don''t
      be afraid to get dirty or wet'
  - key: note.note_doctor_dairy_1.page0.0
    value: "   <b>Working page</b>\n\n   The required substance is hidden within
      a heterogeneous suspension. First it must be purified mechanically \u2014 separate
      the binding fraction from the impurities.\n   I have moved the further sequence
      into the laboratory\nprotocol."
  - key: note.note_doctor_dairy_2.page0.0
    value: "   <b>Personal entry</b>\n\n   I was thirteen when my mother had a stroke.
      For a week I sat by her bed, begging her to open her eyes.\n   The doctors
      said there was nothing more they could do. My father said: it is God's will.\n  
      Mother taught that everyone must face the final Trial alone.\n   I became a
      doctor because I could not accept that."
  - key: note.note_generator_1.page0.1
    value: "   My grandfather used to say: \u201CDrink out of order \u2014 and it'll
      jolt you like a current.\u201D \n   And he always lined the bottles up: the
      light ones first, then the mean ones. He never threw the empties away \u2014
      he was fond of the bright labels, couldn't bring himself to. \n   We laughed,
      and he only twirled his mustache. \n   Now I remember it \u2014 and wonder
      what he meant?"
  - key: note.note_generator_2.page0.1
    value: "Congratulations! \nNow you can see the invisible!\n\nOpen the inventory
      and replace the glass on the flashlight.\n\nFind the hidden hints"
  - key: note.note_laboratory_1.page0.1
    value: "   <b>June 3 </b>\n   \n\n   Yesterday I administered the Frontier to
      myself for the first time. My thoughts grew clearer. In a single night I saw
      what must be changed in the formula.\n   Now I understand why ordinary observation
      was\nnot enough.\n   On a healthy brain the drug acts differently. I was right.\n\n                                
      R. Morro"
  - key: note.note_nurcery_room_1.page0.1
    value: "   The doctor left me instructions. The main thing is not to mix up the
      order: heat awakens the compound but does not make it stable. The state achieved
      must still be fixed.\n   He asked me not to trust appearances. Even a mixture
      that looks right may prove useless. Before using it, I must make sure I have
      obtained the true \u201CFrontier.\u201D\n\n   I will be able to prepare the
      compound correctly. But who will confirm that it should be administered at
      all?\n\n                                    <b>C. Wayne</b>"
  - key: note.note_nurcery_room_3.page0.1
    value: '<b>The green giant</b>, with boughs tall as the sky,

      Gives birth
      to a <b>spark</b> in the rustle of <b>oak groves</b>.


      And from the
      <b>bonfire</b>, burnt down to nothing,

      Comes the <b>ash</b>, whose mass
      is heavy.


      In the depths of the <b>earth</b> hides a sturdy <b>shield</b>,

      And
      the cold <b>steel</b> will imagine itself a <b>tear</b>

      When it melts.
      This <b>smooth surface</b>

      Will help the <b>giant</b> rise again.'
  - key: note.note_nurcery_station_1.page0.1
    value: "   \n   <b>November 21</b>\n\n   Mr. Su opened his eyes and asked for
      hot tea. After a month in a coma \u2014 he simply asked for tea.\n   A few
      hours later he lost consciousness again. But Morro is confident: if he could
      be brought back once, he can be kept back.\n   Today, for the first time, I
      believed that I work in a place where the impossible is done.\n\n                                  
      C. Wayne"
  - key: note.note_procedural_1.page0.1
    value: "   \n   <b>June 14 </b>\n\n   Before Stephanie's last injection, the
      staff argued with Morro. I begged them to trust him one more time.\n   A little
      over an hour later she stopped responding.\n   I keep repeating that I tried
      to stop him. Yet today it was I who persuaded the others to continue.\n\n                                 
      C. Wayne"
  - key: note.note_room2_1.page0.0
    value: Hint 1
  - key: note.note_room2_1.page0.1
    value: "Red \u2014 the Infant,<br>Yellow \u2014 the Youth,\nThe Blue Old Man
      \u2014 and life's thread is spent.\nAnd between them \u2014 Maturity grows:\nYellow
      plus Blue \u2014 Green bestows."
  - key: note.note_room3_1.page0.1
    value: "\t\n\n   The key is hidden in the Spiral of Life. The architect of the
      universe built no straight lines. He coiled the nautilus shell, the pinecones
      and the distant galaxies by one unwavering law of growth. \n   Step into the
      void (0), become the unit (1), repeat yourself (1)... \n   and then let the
      memory of the two last steps beget the third"
  - key: note.note_room3_2.page0.1
    value: "   \n   <b>Patient No. 3 </b>\n\n   Today Anna was nearly screaming,
      trying to count the rhythms of all\nthe instruments at once.\n   Clara asks
      for a pause. She sees overload. I see\nresistance before the final barrier.\n  
      Increase the dose.\n   They look at the readings but do not see the whole picture.\n\n                                
      R. Morro"
  - key: note.note_room4_1.page0
    value: 'You need to find the time...

      Set the correct time...

      Three
      are there, one more remains...'
  - key: note.note_room5_1.page0.0
    value: The three principal laws of the energy flow
  - key: note.note_room5_1.page0.1
    value: "   <b>Continuity of the current</b>\n   Energy flows strictly along the
      tracing of the rune \u2014 from origin to completion. It is forbidden to break
      the flow, return to a link already passed, or \u201Crewrite\u201D the line
      backward. The movement of magic is forward only, along the spiral of the pattern.\n\n  
      <b>Smoothness of the lines</b>\n   Runic script does not tolerate angular kinks
      or unnatural breaks. All transitions between runes must be smooth, as if drawn
      with a single stroke of the brush. The joint must preserve the integrity of
      the arc, without sharp \u201Csteps\u201D or sudden changes of direction.\n\n  
      <b>Sacred order</b>\n   The master must activate the runes in exactly the order
      prescribed by the scroll-task. Not a single rune may be skipped, rearranged
      or replaced with an analogous one \u2014 otherwise the formula will lose its
      power. Only strict adherence to the chain of signs allows the true magic circle
      to be closed."
